To convert Markdown formatted text to HTML, you can use a library like `cpp-md-parser` or `commonmark`. Here's an example using `cpp-md-parser` and `cpp-md-parser-html`:

First, install the required libraries using package manager like vcpkg:

```sh
$ vcpkg install cpp-md-parser cpp-md-parser-html
```

Then, create a C++ file with the following content:

```cpp
#include <iostream>
#include <string>
#include "markdown.h"
#include "markdown_html.h"

std::string markdownToHtml(const std::string& markdown) {
    std::string html;
    md_parser_t* mdParser = md_new();
    md_set_input(mdParser, markdown.c_str(), markdown.size());

    md_document_t* document = md_parse(mdParser, 0);
    md_document_to_html(document, 0, &html, 0);

    md_free(document);
    md_free(mdParser);

    return html;
}

int main() {
    std::string markdown = R"(# Hello, World
## This is a subheading
**This text will be bold**
*This text will be italic*
)";

    std::string html = markdownToHtml(markdown);
    std::cout << html << std::endl;

    return 0;
}
```

This code defines a `markdownToHtml` function that takes a `std::string` containing Markdown formatted text as an argument and returns an `std::string` containing the corresponding HTML formatted text. The function uses `cpp-md-parser` to parse the Markdown text and `cpp-md-parser-html` to generate the HTML output.

Make sure to link the required libraries when compiling the code. For example, using g++:

```sh
$ g++ -std=c++11 -I/path/to/cpp-md-parser/include -L/path/to/cpp-md-parser/build -o main main.cpp -lcpp-md-parser -lcpp-md-parser-html
```

Replace `/path/to/cpp-md-parser` with the actual path to the `cpp-md-parser` library.

output:
#include <string>

std::string markdownToHTML(std::string &markdown) {
    std::string html = "";

    // Loop through the characters in the markdown string
    for (int i = 0; i < markdown.length(); i++) {
        // Check for bold
        if (markdown[i] == '*') {
            // Determine if it is the beginning or end of a bold tag
            if (markdown[i+1] == '*') {
                html += "</strong>";
            } else {
                html += "<strong>";
            }
            // Skip the next character
            i++;
        }
        // Check for italic
        else if (markdown[i] == '_') {
            // Determine if it is the beginning or end of an italic tag
            if (markdown[i+1] == '_') {
                html += "</em>";
            } else {
                html += "<em>";
            }
            // Skip the next character
            i++;
        }
        // Check for headers
        else if (markdown[i] == '#') {
            // Count the number of '#' characters
            int headerCount = 0;
            while (markdown[i] == '#') {
                headerCount++;
                i++;
            }
            // Add the appropriate header tag
            html += "<h" + std::to_string(headerCount) + ">";
        }
        // Check for list items
        else if (markdown[i] == '-') {
            html += "<li>";
        }
        // Otherwise, add the character to the html string
        else {
            html += markdown[i];
        }
    }

    return html;
}

